cards.definition:
A pair of linear equations in two variables is consistent if there exists at least one ordered pair (x, y) that satisfies both equations simultaneously; it is inconsistent if no such ordered pair exists. For equations \(a_1x + b_1y + c_1 = 0\) and \(a_2x + b_2y + c_2 = 0\) with \(a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2 
eq 0\), the system is consistent with a unique solution when \( rac{a_1}{a_2} 
eq  rac{b_1}{b_2}\), consistent with infinitely many solutions (dependent) when \( rac{a_1}{a_2} =  rac{b_1}{b_2} =  rac{c_1}{c_2}\), and inconsistent when \( rac{a_1}{a_2} =  rac{b_1}{b_2} 
eq  rac{c_1}{c_2}\).
